Moroccan security forces displayed "total permissiveness" during last month's massive wave of migrants who crossed into the Spanish North African territory of Ceuta, according to a Spanish police report seen by a French news agency on Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cf6d932-a517-11f1-b815-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26233420530465.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cf6d932-a517-11f1-b815-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26233420530465.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1ffac56a-a702-11f1-a811-33773faa09bf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 19:20:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cf6d932-a517-11f1-b815-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26233420530465.jpg">© Antonio Sempere, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Live: Macron and Charles III visit historic Bayeux tapestry exhibition together</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-france-s-macron-in-britain-to-help-unveil-bayeux-tapestry</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">0492aa12-a6f9-11f1-9083-2ff77675d9fc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 18:09:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Israeli FM Gideon Sa'ar: 'I hope Iran will not make the mistake of attacking us'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260902-israeli-fm-gideon-sa-ar-i-hope-iran-will-not-make-the-mistake-of-attacking-us</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israel's Minister of Foreign Affairs Gideon Sa’ar addressed the resumption in fighting between the US and Iran, and warned that any Iranian attack on Israel would trigger a "severe" response. He also accused Tehran of continuing to pursue "nuclear weapons aspirations", claiming that Israel "will not allow" Iran to achieve them. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be03f3b8-a6e8-11f1-aab9-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/TAT-SAAR-POUR-MIX.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be03f3b8-a6e8-11f1-aab9-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/TAT-SAAR-POUR-MIX.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed61f0d6-a6e0-11f1-b900-bbccc4313f26</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 17:49:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Videos and debris raise questions over alleged US strike on Iranian wedding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-videos-and-debris-raise-questions-over-alleged-us-strike-on-iranian-wedding</link><description>
On the evening of September 1, a barrage of US missile and drone attacks on a town in southern Iran allegedly struck a wedding ceremony, killing at least five people, including a four-year-old boy. FRANCE 24 geolocated a direct hit to the civilian building where local residents say the wedding was being held. The building was more than 135 meters from the apparent target, a communications tower.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1586076a-a6e5-11f1-9f77-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-02-at-5-42-07-PM.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1586076a-a6e5-11f1-9f77-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-02-at-5-42-07-PM.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">78860efa-a6ea-11f1-875a-ab9559766e7b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 17:31:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1586076a-a6e5-11f1-9f77-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-02-at-5-42-07-PM.png">© Screengrab 7sobh</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia blamed for explosive-laden drone found at German airport</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-russia-blamed-for-explosive-laden-drone-found-at-german-airport</link><description>
After #Germany blamed #Russia for the explosive-laden #drone found at #Leipzig airport on August 4, #Berlin has introduced new sanctions against #Moscow. Namely, its consulate in #Bonn and the Russian House - a cultural centre thought to be a Russian #spy hub - in #Berlin.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6795890-a6e7-11f1-80d6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-Leipzig.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6795890-a6e7-11f1-80d6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-Leipzig.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8f38202-a6e7-11f1-837e-cd8816f6a8c6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 16:11:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Live: Trump suggests renaming Hormuz 'Trump Strait'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-us-military-striking-targets-in-iran-after-attempted-attacks-on-shipping</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">41d57eaa-a6e4-11f1-8bc1-db6ab52f1458</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 15:37:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Egypt welcomes Xi as Beijing expands influence in region</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-egypt-welcomes-xi-as-beijing-expands-influence-in-region</link><description>
Egyptian ​President Abdel Fattah al-Sisi welcomed China's Xi Jinping to Cairo on Wednesday, opening a visit that highlights Cairo's deepening ties with Beijing as regional turmoil prompts U.S. allies to reassess longstanding security relationships.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5345086-a6e2-11f1-b02a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-163722-163918-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5345086-a6e2-11f1-b02a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-163722-163918-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f9fae198-a6e2-11f1-af78-bbccc4313f26</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 15:33:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Philippine couple married in hip-deep floodwaters</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-philippine-couple-married-in-hip-deep-floodwaters</link><description>
A Philippine couple tied the knot on Tuesday at a Catholic church swamped in hip-deep waters, as heavy rains had pummelled large parts of the country for a month.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7030a242-a6e0-11f1-80ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7030a242-a6e0-11f1-80ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84ba1356-a6e0-11f1-802a-c1762cef3722</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 15:21:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US postal whistleblower warns thousands of midterm ballots could be lost</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-us-postal-whistleblower-warns-thousands-of-midterm-ballots-could-be-lost</link><description>
A US Postal Service whistleblower has warned that millions of Americans could be prevented from receiving mail ballots ahead of November's midterm elections because of a rushed, new system ordered by President Donald Trump and due for launch Tuesday. Trump signed an executive order in March seeking tighter controls on mail voting, which he has repeatedly claimed is vulnerable to widespread fraud despite offering no evidence of misconduct on such a scale. France 24’s Kethevane Gorjestani takes a closer look.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/31b1d516-a6dd-11f1-85d3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-161238-161837-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/31b1d516-a6dd-11f1-85d3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-161238-161837-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">67424d78-a6dd-11f1-b09c-c1762cef3722</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 15:17:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Search continues for tunnel workers in Nepal floods</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-search-continues-for-tunnel-workers-in-nepal-floods</link><description>
Nepali authorities believe that the dozens of workers trapped in hydropower tunnels could still be alive, as some of the tunnels have chambers with air supplies. But rescue teams are still struggling, with difficult weather and heavy rains worsening the situation, reports France 24's Shahzaib Wahlah.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a05aa30-a5ef-11f1-a454-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T073115Z-850354389-RC2I9NA94M1D-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a05aa30-a5ef-11f1-a454-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T073115Z-850354389-RC2I9NA94M1D-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">128287b6-a6de-11f1-ae1c-1118e1e87163</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 15:17:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>George Clooney, Robert Pattinson expected on the red carpet at Venice Film Festival</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260902-george-clooney-robert-pattinson-expected-on-the-red-carpet-at-venice-film-festival</link><description>
Our film critic Emma Jones takes us through the highlights as the 83rd Venice International Film Festival kicks off this Wednesday. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8762452-a6d4-11f1-bf12-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12733701466a9828bde5ec76-47150554.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8762452-a6d4-11f1-bf12-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12733701466a9828bde5ec76-47150554.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dd934f0c-a6d5-11f1-a169-c3a5f90ffaca</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 14:56:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel ‘organised and prepared’ to remove Gaza population if US gives green light, Katz says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-israel-organised-and-prepared-to-remove-gaza-population-if-us-gives-green-light-katz</link><description>
Israel is "organised and prepared" to remove Palestininians from Gaza "by every way possible", Defence Minister Israel Katz told reporters Wednesday, adding that there was no alternative "solution" to crisis. The Israeli government was simply waiting for the US to figure out where to take the displaced Gazans, he said.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dba92900-ab4a-11f0-9ad3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25288675368685.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dba92900-ab4a-11f0-9ad3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25288675368685.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a1eebe0-a6db-11f1-b041-c1762cef3722</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 14:56:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dba92900-ab4a-11f0-9ad3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25288675368685.jpg">AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Paradox of Balladur's legacy: 'Highly popular' innovative Gaullist gradually became irrelevant</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/paradox-of-balladur-s-legacy-highly-popular-gaullist-elite-yet-too-far-away-from-the-people</link><description>
Sharon Gaffney is pleased to welcome Renaud Foucart, Senior Lecturer at Lancaster University. According to Foucart, Édouard Balladur’s political legacy mattered because he embodied a political model that was innovative and yet limited in scope and longevity. As PM under Socialist President François Mitterrand, Balladur helped demonstrate that ideological rivals could govern together under cohabitation while pursuing an ambitious programme of privatisation and economic reform. Yet Foucart argues that Balladur’s ultimately unsuccessful presidential campaign exposed a deeper transformation in French politics: technocratic competence, elite stature and institutional authority were becoming less electorally powerful than the ability to connect with ordinary voters. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d7d6e10-a6d4-11f1-ab27-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260831-233408-234033-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d7d6e10-a6d4-11f1-ab27-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260831-233408-234033-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">24e05a14-a6d4-11f1-9e5b-e145f444c45c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 14:29:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Xi calls on Mideast nations to be ‘masters of their own affairs’ in rare Egypt visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-xi-calls-on-mideast-nations-to-be-masters-of-their-own-affairs-in-rare-egypt-visit</link><description>
Chinese President Xi Jinping on Wednesday called on "the people of the Middle East" to oppose "externalinterference" and consider reshaping the region's security order during a visit to Egypt. The rare visit by the Chinese leader comes as Beijing aims to expand its influence in the region as the Iran war tests the reliability of the traditional US security umbrella in a vital geostrategic zone. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7787cb1e-a6d2-11f1-88a1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26244634219317.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7787cb1e-a6d2-11f1-88a1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26244634219317.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21d90a86-a6d5-11f1-8697-c3a5f90ffaca</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 14:22:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7787cb1e-a6d2-11f1-88a1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26244634219317.jpg">© Khaled Desouki, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French president to open Bayeux Tapestry exhibition as he starts UK visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-french-president-to-open-bayeux-tapestry-exhibition-as-he-starts-uk-visit</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron begins a two-day visit to Britain on Wednesday, viewing the landmark Bayeux Tapestry exhibition with King Charles III and becoming the first EU leader to be hosted by Prime Minister Andy Burnham. The tapestry depicts the Norman conquest of England in 1066. In the post-Brexit era, "the loaning of the tapestry is a great example of French-British cooperation" said Burnham.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3383fb0-7c54-11f1-ba24-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Bayeux-tapestry-000-1K924I.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3383fb0-7c54-11f1-ba24-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Bayeux-tapestry-000-1K924I.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3900ec48-a6d4-11f1-adf9-c3a5f90ffaca</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 14:06:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>France's back-to-school challenges: Phones, payslips, pupils</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260902-france-s-back-to-school-challenges-phones-payslips-pupils</link><description>
First day of school jitters are now behind most of France's 11.6 million pupils, but this "rentrée", or back-to-school period, is being marked by a number of challenges and changes: phone bans, concerns over sexual abuse, teachers' salaries, and 161,000 fewer students due to France's falling birthrate. We take a closer look in Entre Nous.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/746325b0-a6d1-11f1-bc07-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15420667106a982343194ad2-24725576.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/746325b0-a6d1-11f1-bc07-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15420667106a982343194ad2-24725576.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c1f09924-a6d2-11f1-8302-c3a5f90ffaca</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 14:04:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Solange MOUGIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>FRANCE 24 in Nepal: The unbearable wait for missing relatives</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-france-24-in-nepal-the-unbearable-wait-for-missing-relatives</link><description>
In Nepal, the hope of finding survivors is fading daily. Bodies are piling up in morgues, and storage capacity is reaching its limit. For the relatives of the missing, the wait is unbearable. They go from one hospital to another, consult the lists of survivors and scrutinise the photos of unidentified bodies. FRANCE 24's special correspondents met with several of these families at the morgue of Kathmandu University Hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f3774cc-a6d4-11f1-9f06-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mini2-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f3774cc-a6d4-11f1-9f06-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mini2-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">971a982e-a6d4-11f1-9051-c3a5f90ffaca</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 14:03:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Dangerous consequences': Iran warns US after alleged strike on wedding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-dangerous-consequences-iran-warns-us-after-alleged-strike-on-wedding</link><description>
Iran has launched strikes towards US allies in the Gulf this Wednesday after US bombardment that Tehran said hit a wedding party, killing five people and wounding dozens. The latest escalation appears to have hardened the mood in the Islamic Republic, with authorities warning American allies in the region they're fair game.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92ae7028-a6d2-11f1-905c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-143255-143422-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92ae7028-a6d2-11f1-905c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-143255-143422-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9765ba5e-a6d2-11f1-a275-e145f444c45c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 13:43:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French-Saudi ‘Dragon Ball’ theme park puzzles Japanese manga fans</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260902-french-saudi-dragon-ball-theme-park-puzzles-japan-manga-fans</link><description>
Plans to build a manga-themed park outside Paris have sparked excitement in France, one of the first Western countries to fall in love with Akira Toriyama’s iconic “Dragon Ball” franchise. Saudi bankrolling of the project, however, and the lack of response from Japanese licence holders, have raised eyebrows among experts and fans alike.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63b876e6-a6c9-11f1-a3bc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2248783613.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63b876e6-a6c9-11f1-a3bc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2248783613.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0ab299a8-a6c1-11f1-bfeb-d1be7233563a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 13:42:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63b876e6-a6c9-11f1-a3bc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2248783613.jpg">© Michael Loccisano, Getty Images via AFP</source><dc:creator>Benjamin DODMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Macron set to unveil Bayeux Tapestry in 'once in a generation' UK loan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-macron-set-to-unveil-bayeux-tapestry-in-once-in-a-generation-uk-loan</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron is set to assist in the unveiling of the Bayeux Tapestry as it goes on show in the UK as part of a historic loan to the British Museum on Wednesday. Macron is on a two-day visit to the UK where he will become the first EU leader to meet new Prime Minister Andy Burnham in Downing Street.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a9195686-a6d0-11f1-80d0-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-141329-141751-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a9195686-a6d0-11f1-80d0-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-141329-141751-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ae3cf56e-a6d0-11f1-80b9-8b24b0a5f6e0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 13:39:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal floods: Hundreds of unidentified bodies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-nepal-floods-hundreds-of-unidentified-bodies</link><description>
France 24's Shahzaib Wahlah reports from Kathmandu, Nepal, after visiting hospitals and morgues in the city struggling to cope with the influx of dead from the devastating floods that hit the country a week ago. Authorities have now begun taking DNA samples from the relatives of the missing in the hope of identifying the bodies as the hope of finding more survivors fades.
